  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_d4e2e3e08e7a48be997115907b02de89",
      "statement": "PRISM Payments Hub (PPH) tracks each wire through thirteen canonical v2 lifecycle states - RECEIVED, VALIDATING, SCREENING, HELD, REPAIR, FUNDS_CONTROL, WAREHOUSED, RELEASED, SENT_TO_NETWORK, NETWORK_ACCEPTED, NETWORK_REJECTED, COMPLETED, CANCELLED, and RETURNED - exposed via the v2 payment-detail API and the pay.wire.lifecycle.v2 Kafka topic.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L54-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe959f59a4c9193850c9329f96b0e9b0dee89db60bf681e8209d7555f9c5042c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9503554d7ac34448aa4e079591710b78",
      "statement": "The legacy v1 wire status API (GET /pph/v1/wires/{wireRef}/status) exposes only seven coarse status values (RECEIVED, PENDING, HELD, PROCESSED, REJECTED, CANCELLED, RETURNED) and collapses the v2 states RELEASED, SENT_TO_NETWORK, NETWORK_ACCEPTED, and COMPLETED into the single value PROCESSED, so v1 consumers cannot distinguish a wire that has merely been released from one acknowledged by the network or closed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-api-cat-2026.3-prism-payments-hub-api-and-event-catalog.md#L45-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:287cfab04f755c79e9f79c9e8e4faf37a02d4a030b1ec484e0470c61a14a2c12:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L84-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:21738d3037172c3ba6816e77abf591c6152ee6ae1e7ab488a7c1e382e9d03f23:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_edaa031f118843c7abb852cbd12ee1ef",
      "statement": "NETWORK_ACCEPTED has rail-specific business meaning: on Fedwire Funds it reflects a Federal Reserve pacs.002 positive acknowledgment carrying OMAD representing final, irrevocable interbank settlement (but not beneficiary credit), while on Swift CBPR+ it reflects only a SwiftNet delivery ACK with no settlement implication, with beneficiary credit knowable only via a Swift gpi ACCC status if available. The v2 stateHistory timestamp for NETWORK_ACCEPTED is PPH's processing time, not the Federal Reserve's pacs.002 creation timestamp.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pph-sys-ovw-9.2-prism-payments-hub-system-overview-and-lifecycle-state-model.md#L88-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e075ddaf74fe14ef25d7654439b547f620a93a40fb689563c40fbfb4f7605d8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_adc259323f624671a6506b09152390d0",
      "statement": "A production client complaint (CMP-2026-1189) arose because a EUR 412,600 international wire showed v1 status PROCESSED (displayed to the client as 'Completed') on 2026-09-16, was then rejected by the beneficiary bank (pacs.002 RJCT, reason AC04) on 2026-09-17, and funds were returned on 2026-09-21; the client had already released goods based on the 'Completed' label.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/jira-export-wt-discovery-2026-10-05.md#L101-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5ed62ff0a6bb02c125cfdd5f85afddbf088d43fecf00f00f5e7301e2ecf9406:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/jira-export-wt-discovery-2026-10-05.md#L187-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:91ed8f7fa079b70de3d33eb0361dd8bed242d2c8a60fba76360f803c83e4aa0c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/jira-export-wt-discovery-2026-10-05.md#L36-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:66fa16158f30910f618d8f4aa88b9406d6dd7fb535cb1d535d9c6e9fb99d1324:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_79522de4d84241359e6603f0de472f38",
      "statement": "The 2024 Wire Status Lite pilot (PIR-2024-07, INC-2024-1182) found that 37% of surveyed pilot users believed the v1 'Processed' status meant the beneficiary had already received the funds, and the pilot's 30-second polling of the v1 status API drove ~85 TPS that exhausted PPH's API thread pool at month-end, delaying release of 1,240 wires by 47 minutes and causing 312 wires to miss the Fedwire cutoff; the v1 status API was subsequently rate-limited to 20 TPS shared across all consumers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pir-2024-07-wire-status-lite-pilot-inc-2024-1182-post-implementation-review.md#L24-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:056800b306805720e84936c3fc3297ad7b26acaa3265204fb60d04e4a39d631f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a9d2c484b1454643829b3df9dbb500d9",
      "statement": "The v1 status API's holdReasonDesc field carries a free-text HMS hold description synchronized for backward compatibility with the Wire Room console (not curated for external display) and is absent from v2, which instead exposes only hold.isHeld and hold.holdId; the v1 fedRef field carries only the IMAD, with OMAD and UETR never exposed in v1.",
      "evidence": [
